 366.91  11:20:48  The mechanical clock escapement serves as the beating heart of horological precision. This ingenious device acts as both an energy regulator and a timekeeper, controlling the release of stored power from a mainspring or hanging weight while simultaneously counting time intervals through rhythmic oscillation.
 379.42  11:20:48
 379.42  11:21:06  At its core, the escapement consists primarily of two interlocking components: the escape wheel - a toothed gear driven by the clock's main power source - and one or more pallets attached to an oscillating element like a pendulum or balance wheel. These parts engage in a precisely choreographed dance, allowing just enough energy to pass through each cycle while preventing backsliding that would compromise accuracy.
