 406.22  11:21:15  || === AC 10 above: did a scheduled turn cut into that reply, or wait for it? ===
 398.08  11:21:27  When the escape wheel's teeth attempt to advance forward, they are blocked by a pallet surface held in position by the oscillator's momentum. This locking action effectively stops the entire gear train until the oscillating element swings to its opposite position, momentarily releasing the next tooth. The energy stored from each release propels the pendulum or balance through its full arc, while gravity's pull - or torsion spring tension - returns it to restart the cycle.
 418.92  11:21:27
 418.92  11:21:43  This elegant self-sustaining system transforms continuous stored power into regulated intermittent motion. Each oscillation represents one second (for a seconds pendulum) and advances the clock hand by exactly one tick-tock interval. The rate at which these cycles occur determines timekeeping accuracy - too slow and the clock loses ground, too fast and it gains hours.
 435.20  11:21:43
 435.20  11:21:56  Early verge escapements were crude but functional, while later anchor and cylinder designs provided smoother operation with less friction. Today's clocks employ refined versions of this mechanism that has remained fundamentally unchanged since medieval times, proving that elegant simplicity often trumps technological complexity in mechanical engineering.
